{"name":"Yellow Brick Road","hex":"#eac853","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow brick road","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A proverbial path to a Promised Land of one's hopes and dreams."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow_brick_road"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yellow brick road","blocks":[{"text":"The yellow brick road is a central element in the 1900 children's novel The Wonderful Wizard of Oz by American author L. Frank Baum. It also appears in several sequel Oz books such as The Marvelous Land of Oz (1904) and The Patchwork Girl of Oz (1913)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Cowardly_lion2.jpg/330px-Cowardly_lion2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_brick_road"},{"title":"Yellow brick road (mathematics)","blocks":[{"text":"A Yellow brick road is \"the unique simple closed path that solves the antisocial jogger problem for any of the Platonic solids. Such a path must (1) begin and end at a single vertex of the solid, and (2) be a straight line path that may cross over edges, but may not pass through any other vertices.\" The solution for the dodecahedron was given by mathematicians Jayadev Athreya and David Aulicino in a paper published 11 February 2019, and its area division was given by Li Zhou in a paper published 11 October 2021."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_brick_road_(mathematics)"},{"title":"MC4 (mixtape)","blocks":[{"text":"MC4 is the twenty-first mixtape by American rapper French Montana. MC4 was originally intended to be released as his second studio album. It was released on November 5, 2016, by Coke Boys Records, Bad Boy Records, Maybach Music Group and Epic Records. However, the album's release was canceled after Target unofficially released the album on CD on its original release date of August 19, 2016, two months before the album was set to release, which was later leaked online in its entirety. Subsequently, the album was heavily bootlegged. It was French Montana's last project released by Maybach Music Group before leaving the label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/MC4CoverArt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MC4_(mixtape)"},{"title":"Road surface","blocks":[{"text":"A road surface or pavement is the durable surface material laid down on an area intended to sustain vehicular or foot traffic, such as a road or walkway. In the past, gravel road surfaces, macadam, hoggin, cobblestone and sett granite were extensively used, but these have mostly been replaced by asphalt or concrete laid on a compacted base course. Asphalt mixtures have been used in pavement construction since the beginning of the 20th century and are of two types: metalled (hard-surfaced) and unmetalled roads. Metalled roadways are made to sustain vehicular load and so are usually made on frequently used roads. Unmetalled roads, also known as gravel roads or dirt roads, are rough and can sustain less weight. Road surfaces are frequently marked to guide traffic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Road_resurfacing.jpg/330px-Road_resurfacing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road_surface"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg/500px-2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg/1280px-2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg/500px-2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red surfacing for a bicycle lane in the Netherlands","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg/500px-Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg/1280px-Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg/500px-Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Construction crew laying down asphalt over fiber-optic trench, in New York City","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg/500px-Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg/1280px-Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg/500px-Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut